in our broom closet.

643
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:00,941
(COFFEE CARAFE THUDS)

644
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:03,652
It's almost as if
he wanted to get arrested...

645
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:06,155
- (DOOR OPENS)
- ...so I'd throw him in jail
next to the suspect

646
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:08,491
- I told him he couldn't talk to.
- (DOOR CLOSES)

647
00:31:08,492 --> 00:31:11,202
JOHN: I did tell him
it was a stupid plan.

648
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:13,496
- (MUG THUDS)
- You should have
told him louder.

649
00:31:13,497 --> 00:31:16,666
Well, listen, may I take
my stupid friend home?

650
00:31:17,793 --> 00:31:20,044
Not until he's arraigned.

651
00:31:20,045 --> 00:31:23,422
(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

652
00:31:23,423 --> 00:31:24,757
Really?

653
00:31:24,758 --> 00:31:27,093
JUDGE: ...and eight counts
of aggravated assault

654
00:31:27,094 --> 00:31:28,427
and resisting arrest.

655
00:31:28,428 --> 00:31:29,845
How does the defendant plead?

656
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:32,474
HAL: With all due respect,
Your Honor, come on.

657
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:34,392
"Come on"?

658
00:31:34,393 --> 00:31:36,394
Look, I'm just trying
to question a suspect

659
00:31:36,395 --> 00:31:38,270
in the course
of a very serious investigation,

660
00:31:38,271 --> 00:31:40,065
- which I--
- JUDGE: Ah, an investigation.

661
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:42,149
Am I to understand, sir,

662
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:44,485
that you are
a law enforcement official?

663
00:31:44,486 --> 00:31:46,529
And if so, could you kindly
state for the record

664
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:48,281
which agency you represent?

665
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:50,908
I'm Green Lantern.

666
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,618
JUDGE:
I didn't ask who you were.

667
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:55,746
I asked which bureau
you are an agent of.

668
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:56,997
I'm Green Lantern,

669
00:31:56,998 --> 00:31:58,834
and I'm an agent of...

670
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,293
the Green Lantern... s.

671
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:04,296
Look, I introduced myself
to Lady Justice back here

672
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:05,673
when I got to the crime scene,

673
00:32:05,674 --> 00:32:07,842
and I deferred
to her jurisdiction.

674
00:32:07,843 --> 00:32:09,885
Is that accurate, Sheriff?

675
00:32:09,886 --> 00:32:13,389
Yeah, but the deference
was pretty cheeky, Your Honor.

676
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:15,141
- You cheeky, Mr. Jordan?
- (DOOR OPENS)

677
00:32:15,142 --> 00:32:18,060
- WILLIAM "BILLY" MACON:
Yeah, don't-- don't answer that.
- (DOOR CLOSES)

678
00:32:18,061 --> 00:32:20,646
(CLEARS THROAT) William Macon
for the defense, Your Honor.

679
00:32:20,647 --> 00:32:22,565
- Sorry I'm late.
- JUDGE: Mr. Macon.

680
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:25,526
The defendant has chosen
to represent himself.

681
00:32:25,527 --> 00:32:27,027
That's only because
he doesn't understand

682
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:30,197
he's being made an example of,
which, Your Honor,

683
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:33,284
is absurd given Mr. Jordan
is a hero.

684
00:32:33,285 --> 00:32:36,370
Granted, he hasn't, uh,
formally retained my--

685
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,914
- You're hired. He's hired.
- Fantastic.

686
00:32:38,915 --> 00:32:41,333
The defense enters a plea
of not guilty

687
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:44,003
and asks Your Honor
to set reasonable bail,

688
00:32:44,004 --> 00:32:47,757
even understanding Mr. Jordan
is... technically a flight risk.

689
00:32:48,258 --> 00:32:49,134
Because...

690
00:32:50,051 --> 00:32:51,594
he can fly.

691
00:32:51,595 --> 00:32:53,513
- (QUIETLY) Who is this guy?
- (SCOFFS)

692
00:32:54,014 --> 00:32:55,222
My husband.

693
00:32:55,223 --> 00:32:57,600
JUDGE: I'm setting bail
at 100,000 dollars.

694
00:32:57,601 --> 00:33:00,352
- Oh, come on.
- JUDGE: Two hundred thousand.

695
00:33:00,353 --> 00:33:04,106
Now you know the price
of each "come on," Mr. Jordan.

696
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:06,609
- Shall we try another?
- No, that's understood.

697
00:33:06,610 --> 00:33:08,110
And thank you, Your Honor.

698
00:33:08,111 --> 00:33:11,489
My father will have the check
to your clerk by lunch.

699
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:14,950
All right, then.
Mr. Jordan, don't leave town.

700
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:16,453
- We're adjourned.
- (GAVEL THUDS)

701
00:33:18,413 --> 00:33:21,290
- Uh, thanks for the save.
- Oh, truly an honor.

702
00:33:21,291 --> 00:33:23,667
But I tend to find
that strangers who give me

703
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:25,044
a couple
hundred thousand dollars,

704
00:33:25,045 --> 00:33:26,086
no strings attached,

705
00:33:26,087 --> 00:33:28,297
usually turn out to be bad guys.

706
00:33:28,298 --> 00:33:31,133
Uh, but there are
strings attached, Mr. Jordan.

707
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:32,801
My father would love
to have supper

708
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:35,054
with you this evening.
Um, he's a huge fan,

709
00:33:35,055 --> 00:33:37,932
and someone I think
you'll find like-minded.

710
00:33:37,933 --> 00:33:39,141
What are you doing, Billy?

711
00:33:39,142 --> 00:33:40,851
Uh, I was just
inviting Mr. Jordan

712
00:33:40,852 --> 00:33:42,896
up to the ranch tonight, honey.

713
00:33:44,898 --> 00:33:46,357
They're married.

714
00:33:46,358 --> 00:33:49,443
Course, they are.
Small town, everyone's related.

715
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:50,653
Oh.

716
00:33:50,654 --> 00:33:53,280
I'd be offended if that wasn't
absolutely true. (CHUCKLES)

717
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:54,823
Billy Macon, you must be John.

718
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:56,158
- Yes, sir.
- BILLY: You like barbecue?

719
00:33:56,159 --> 00:33:57,910
(SCOFFS) Junior here's a vegan.

720
00:33:57,911 --> 00:33:59,995
He doesn't believe in anything
