HAL: It was a book.

969
00:45:43,199 --> 00:45:44,282
I don't read a lot.

970
00:45:44,283 --> 00:45:45,700
Well, you go
to the movies, don't you?

971
00:45:45,701 --> 00:45:47,202
They only made,
like, 22 of them.

972
00:45:47,203 --> 00:45:49,037
Oh, I watch a lot of football.

973
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:51,539
- HAL: That's the rub, isn't it?
- What?

974
00:45:51,540 --> 00:45:53,583
Pretending to be someone
that you're not.

975
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:54,793
You learn all the specifics,

976
00:45:54,794 --> 00:45:57,379
but you don't learn
what everyone else knows.

977
00:45:57,380 --> 00:45:58,880
Uh... (EXHALES SHARPLY)

978
00:45:58,881 --> 00:46:01,217
I don't-- I don't understand.
Who are you, exactly?

979
00:46:02,718 --> 00:46:04,219
Hal Jordan, Green Lantern.

980
00:46:04,220 --> 00:46:05,595
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

981
00:46:05,596 --> 00:46:07,013
Charged by
the Guardians of the Universe

982
00:46:07,014 --> 00:46:08,473
to protect Sector 2814

983
00:46:08,474 --> 00:46:10,392
from
all extra-planetary threats.

984
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:13,062
And you, Waylon,
are one of them.

985
00:46:14,313 --> 00:46:17,899
Good Christ, he really is
full of himself, isn't he?

986
00:46:17,900 --> 00:46:19,401
Can't be easy,

987
00:46:19,402 --> 00:46:21,903
having to learn
from someone you don't respect.

988
00:46:21,904 --> 00:46:23,571
I do respect him.

989
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:25,157
- KERRY: Come on.
- JOHN: I do.

990
00:46:25,700 --> 00:46:26,741
KERRY: Why?

991
00:46:26,742 --> 00:46:28,910
(HAL CONTINUES
SPEAKING OVER SPEAKER)

992
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:30,578
I don't know. He's fearless.

993
00:46:30,579 --> 00:46:33,248
If you care about people,

994
00:46:33,249 --> 00:46:36,543
you know, husband,
wife, parent, kid,

995
00:46:36,544 --> 00:46:38,753
then you're scared
of losing them.

996
00:46:38,754 --> 00:46:40,380
First time he strutted up to me,

997
00:46:40,381 --> 00:46:44,259
I could tell Jordan doesn't
care about anybody.

998
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:46,594
- And nobody cares about him.
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

999
00:46:46,595 --> 00:46:48,306
He's not fucking fearless.

1000
00:46:48,931 --> 00:46:50,557
He's lonely.

1001
00:46:50,558 --> 00:46:52,350
HAL: <i>But--
But why did you stick around?</i>

1002
00:46:52,351 --> 00:46:53,893
What were you looking for?

1003
00:46:53,894 --> 00:46:55,270
I mean, I get once I showed up,

1004
00:46:55,271 --> 00:46:57,147
you couldn't run.
You had to blend in.

1005
00:46:57,148 --> 00:46:58,273
But before that...

1006
00:46:58,274 --> 00:47:00,608
I just went to a high school
football game, man.

1007
00:47:00,609 --> 00:47:02,736
With the other Kimball fans
who are all dead now.

1008
00:47:02,737 --> 00:47:04,696
WAYLON: I don't know them, okay?

1009
00:47:04,697 --> 00:47:06,114
I told you, I-- I drive a truck.

1010
00:47:06,115 --> 00:47:07,615
HAL: Yeah, I'm sure
you can tell me a lot

1011
00:47:07,616 --> 00:47:09,326
about that truck,
but I bet you can't tell me

1012
00:47:09,327 --> 00:47:11,828
about the Boston Tea Party,
Kelly Clarkson,

1013
00:47:11,829 --> 00:47:13,705
Barack Obama, or Rup--

1014
00:47:13,706 --> 00:47:16,292
Barack Obama is the president
of the United States.

1015
00:47:17,710 --> 00:47:19,294
That's it?

1016
00:47:19,295 --> 00:47:21,504
As a rural Nebraskan,
that's the breadth

1017
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:23,965
of your opinion
of Barack Hussein Obama?

1018
00:47:23,966 --> 00:47:27,427
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

1019
00:47:27,428 --> 00:47:30,138
He is the 44th president.
He followed George W. Bush.

1020
00:47:30,139 --> 00:47:31,431
There's some controversy

1021
00:47:31,432 --> 00:47:33,142
surrounding
his birth certificate.

1022
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:38,564
Holy shit, you are an alien.

1023
00:47:39,607 --> 00:47:41,941
♪ (UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

1024
00:47:41,942 --> 00:47:42,985
(SIGHS)

1025
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:48,491
Let's say you're right.

1026
00:47:49,033 --> 00:47:49,992
Oh, fuck.

1027
00:47:50,826 --> 00:47:52,744
WAYLON:
<i>Let's say, hypothetically,</i>

1028
00:47:52,745 --> 00:47:55,497
that I'm not of this salty,
smelly world,

1029
00:47:55,498 --> 00:47:57,499
a visitor
who went to great trouble

1030
00:47:57,500 --> 00:48:00,085
to hide himself well
and learn the arcane rules

1031
00:48:00,086 --> 00:48:02,003
of pointless contests
involving balls

1032
00:48:02,004 --> 00:48:03,671
that somehow
captivate more attention

1033
00:48:03,672 --> 00:48:05,465
than the
deteriorating atmosphere

1034
00:48:05,466 --> 00:48:07,593
or the hunger
of its least fortunate people.

1035
00:48:10,888 --> 00:48:12,639
If I had gone to such lengths,

1036
00:48:12,640 --> 00:48:14,516
I would be here
for a very important purpose.

1037
00:48:14,517 --> 00:48:17,143
A purpose that required
great discretion and secrecy.

1038
00:48:17,144 --> 00:48:19,104
A purpose that would need
to be kept from the likes

1039
00:48:19,105 --> 00:48:21,272
of a galactic
peacekeeping organization

1040
00:48:21,273 --> 00:48:23,651
because it concerns
the exact opposite of peace.

1041
00:48:24,527 --> 00:48:25,611
That being war.

1042
00:48:26,570 --> 00:48:27,862
And as such,

1043
00:48:27,863 --> 00:48:30,657
if I were to fall into the hands
of such an organization,

1044
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:32,992
I would be forced
to take drastic measures

1045
00:48:32,993 --> 00:48:35,329
to ensure that my purpose
was not revealed.

1046
00:48:37,998 --> 00:48:39,083
Hypothetically.

1047
00:48:44,046 --> 00:48:45,130
And hypothetically,

1048
00:48:45,131 --> 00:48:47,590
what might you have
to keep your mouth shut?

1049
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:50,009
- A cyanide pill?
- You're thinking very small.

1050
00:48:50,010 --> 00:48:51,136
Then give it to me big.

1051
00:48:51,137 --> 00:48:52,887
I'd have
a biometric neutron device

1052
00:48:52,888 --> 00:48:54,139
woven into my skeleton.

1053
00:48:54,140 --> 00:48:55,808
I'd be able to activate it
with a thought.

1054
00:48:57,768 --> 00:49:00,228
<i>Unless you let me walk out
that door right now.</i>

1055
00:49:00,229 --> 00:49:02,021
He's bluffing, right?

1056
00:49:02,022 --> 00:49:04,566
HAL: <i>You're not walking out
of here hypothetically
or otherwise.</i>

1057
00:49:04,567 --> 00:49:07,360
And if you do blow yourself up,
I'm just gonna bubble up

1058
00:49:07,361 --> 00:49:09,571
